            <div class="details">
                <section>
                    <h3 id="stay-title">Where to stay</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Yosemite: campgrounds book out months ahead on Recreation.gov; Curry Village tent cabins</li>
                        <li>Yellowstone: campgrounds inside the park, or motels in West Yellowstone</li>
                        <li>Banff: hostels in Banff town and at Lake Louise</li>
                        <li>Jasper: campgrounds and hostels. Check current conditions, since the 2024 wildfire damaged part of town</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                <aside>
                    <h3 id="glance-title">At a glance</h3>
                    <div class="glance">
                        <p><strong>Best time:</strong> June to September, when the high roads and trails are snow-free.</p>
                        <p><strong>Daily budget:</strong> About $120–180 per person per day, much less if you camp. An annual parks pass covers US park entry.</p>
                        <p><strong>Getting around:</strong> A rental car is essential. Book one-way rentals early, since crossing the border adds fees.</p>
                        <p><strong>Fly in / fly out:</strong> Arrive in San Francisco (SFO) and leave from Edmonton (YEG).</p>
                    </div>
                </aside>
